{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The magnetic hooks match my recent interest in hanging things on magnetic surfaces, so their purpose feels relevant even though I would skip another pack now.",
    "The pegboard hooks connect with my interest in organizing tools, although I would need to confirm that I have a suitable pegboard before choosing them."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Electrical terminals, resistors and hose clamps serve specific tasks I have not shown a need for; buying screws and washers does not make those tasks relevant to me.",
    "The laboratory film, large waste container and foil tape do not address a current need. Separate caster wheels also require a project that my older hand truck purchase does not establish.",
    "Adhesive mounting tape shares a mounting purpose with magnetic hooks, but I have recently chosen magnetic options and have no reason to switch methods now."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My hardware assortment purchases seem to have been taken as interest in almost any repair or project supply, when the actual use matters much more to me.",
    "My hand truck purchase seems to have been stretched into a need for caster wheels, even though buying a complete truck does not mean I am building or repairing rolling equipment."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I recently bought two packs of magnetic hooks, which makes another similar pack less useful despite being a close match to my interests.",
    "I rarely choose supplies without a concrete use, and a possible organizing interest alone is not enough when an item requires equipment such as a compatible pegboard."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognized my interest in practical hardware and organization, but often assumed new project needs and overlooked what I had already bought."
}"}
